WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.720
Missing logs prevent teams from reconstructing important events.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.500
Applications should capture authentication activity, authorization failures,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:13.200
administrative actions, sensitive data access, configuration changes,

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:15.420
and high-risk workflow events.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.520
Poor monitoring leaves teams with telemetry they do not review, alerts they do not trust,

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.860
or events that cannot be correlated across systems.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.200
Monitoring must support timely analysis and response.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.620
Delayed detection increases attacker dwell time and impact.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.600
Without alerting and review, compromise, insider abuse,

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.100
and data access anomalies may continue unnoticed.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.640
Insufficient alerting and log protection can harm both incident response and audit

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:49.020
readiness. Logs need retention, integrity, review ownership, and clear escalation paths.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:55.320
Centralize logs across applications, identity systems, infrastructure, and cloud services.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.580
Integrate telemetry with SIEM or monitoring workflows.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:01.920
Create alerting and review processes for high-risk events.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:11.100
Selected CMMC mappings for this topic include AU.L2-3.3.1 - Audit logging;

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:15.720
AU.L2-3.3.2 - Log review.
